WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-US

00:00:00.920 --> 00:00:06.120
Let’s see how we did in figuring out the&nbsp;
data types for each of these statements.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:13.480
I will run this code, and we will see each&nbsp;
data type listed in the terminal window. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:22.880
first statement is a string, as the data is&nbsp;
in quotes. The second statement is a bool,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:30.720
short for Boolean, as the word True with a capital&nbsp;
T is the value, and we just covered how True and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:40.280
False with title cases represent Booleans. The&nbsp;
third statement is a string, even though we see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:52.800
a number here. Why? Because it is in quotes.&nbsp;
The fourth statement is a float with a decimal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.800 --> 00:01:01.760
and the fifth statement is an integer, as&nbsp;
it is a whole number and not in quotes. 

